          ],
          "correct": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "695b81fd471cd7432e79acc8",
          "question": "<p>Let the normals at points \\( A(4 a,-4 a) \\) and \\( B(9 a,-6 a) \\) on the parabola \\( y^{2}=4 a x \\) meet at the point \\( P \\). The&nbsp;equation of the normal from \\( P \\) on \\( y^{2}=4 a x \\) (other than \\( P A \\) and \\( P B \\) ) is:</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( 5 x+y-135 a=0 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 5 x-y+115 a=0 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 5 x+y+115=0 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 5 x-y-115 a=0 \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "695b81fd471cd7432e79acbd",
          "question": "<p>If two parabola \\( y^{2}=4 a(x-a) \\) and \\( x^{2}=4 a(y-a) \\) have only one common point \\( P \\), then the equation of normal to \\( y^{2}=4 a(x-k) \\) at \\( P \\) is:</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( y+x=4 a \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( y+x=2 a \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( y+x=4 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( y+x=2 \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 0
